WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.980
You can see them everywhere in Lagos: people
relieving themselves outdoors, in the open.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.350
One of every four Nigerians has no access
to a proper toilet.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.790
It has been so difficult for us.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:17.070
What we do is, we come to this river here
to excrete ourselves.”

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:21.109
+++
The way they relieve themselves is disturbing

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:23.070
to those of us living here.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.590
Because out in the open, everyone can see
them.

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:32.400
The government should at least build a cover
so we can’t see them.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.580
It is very difficult for us.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.360
We have to go to the river to poo.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.180
Some women poo inside a bucket, and then dump
it into the river.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.500
It is not good.”+++
20 million people live in this overcrowded

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.500
megacity.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.550
Bad hygiene and a lack of sufficient toilets
are endangering people's health in the poorer

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.550
districts.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.310
Ironically, it's easier to find a mobile phone
than a toilet.

00:00:59.310 --> 00:01:03.450
You find warnings like this everywhere in
Lagos.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.540
And yet they are always ignored.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.760
Because there are simply no alternatives.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.060
The lack of toilets is turning into a big
business for some people.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.150
Jeremiah Jere installed some "porta potties"
near a bus station.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.970
Now he makes about 30 Euros a day.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:28.920
Number one costs 10 cents, number two will
cost

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:29.920
you 25 cents.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.920
It's a good business!

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:34.870
When you come here to relieve yourself, it
will save you from disgrace.

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:40.770
You know, urinating is an emergency sometimes.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:50.159
Most of the time, people in an area like this
relieve themselves anywhere, when it is urgent.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:57.630
But if they begin to feel it gradually, they
can come to this place.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:00.600
This is where Jere's toilets are produced.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:05.799
Lanre Akinwale's company is the only one in
Nigeria that builds mobile toilets.

00:02:05.799 --> 00:02:09.230
It employs thirty-one people, and business
is booming.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:14.860
With a population of almost 200 million, Nigeria
provides a huge market for his product.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:19.850
Still, Akinwale is troubled by the current
situation, and says the government alone,

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.040
is not to blame.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.430
We need to begin to change the mentality of
the people.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:31.340
Even if you tell some people go and use the
toilet, they will tell you that they prefer

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:32.340
to go into the bush.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.150
They prefer it, because the breeze is blowing
there.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:35.680
That’s the mentality.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:38.980
But it is not good for us.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:50.190
So at it is now, we need to put on some strict
measures to stop this open defecation.

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:53.120
The government did create an emergency plan.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.980
But up until now, almost nothing has changed.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:01.370
The toilet crisis in Lagos clearly remains
a problem that needs an urgent solution.

